SOURCE_TITLE=Small generators of the ideal class group
AUTHORS=Karim Belabas; Francisco Diaz y Diaz; Eduardo Friedman
PUBLICATION=Mathematics of Computation 77 (2008), 1185-1197
DOI=10.1090/S0025-5718-07-02003-0
SOURCE_URL=https://www.math.u-bordeaux.fr/~kbelabas/research/OnBach.pdf
SOURCE_PDF_SHA256=e619d0f0c52bfddd0316e354d72c1b3b7946d85a1cdcbad05aac990cf911fc78
SOURCE_LOCATION=Section 5; Theorem 5.1; Corollary 5.2; equations (23)-(24)

AUDITED_STATEMENT:
For every T>1, if the strict inequality in Corollary 5.2 holds, then the
classes of all prime ideals of K having norm strictly less than T generate
the full ideal class group.  Section 5 explicitly drops GRH.  This p=31
scout uses only the positive sub-sum from degree-one prime ideals, with every
power whose norm is strictly less than T=40000000.  It does not construct or
verify principal-ideal witnesses and it does not make any claim if the
strict RealBall margin is nonpositive.

FIELD_LEDGER:
K=Q(alpha), alpha^31=2.  Since 2^30 mod 31^2 is 187, not 1, the standard
pure-prime-degree index criterion gives O_K=Z[alpha].  Thus the field degree
is 31, the signature is (1,15), and |Delta_K|=2^30*31^31.
